{"etape": 9, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-27T12:03:00.639088Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "I checked the options for your dates, but there's an important constraint I need to flag.\n\nYour reservation **K1NW8N** is booked in **basic economy**, and per policy, **basic economy flights cannot be modified** — the flight segments themselves can't be changed. What *is* allowed is a **cabin upgrade to business while keeping the exact same flights**.\n\nHere's what that would look like (all 3 passengers, business class):\n\n| Flight | Route | Date | Business price |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| HAT023 | JFK → SFO | 2024-05-26 | $364 |\n| HAT204 | SFO → SEA | 2024-05-28 | $248 |\n| HAT021 | SEA → JFK | 2024-05-28 | $453 |\n\n- **Per passenger:** $1,065\n- **Total for 3 passengers:** $3,195\n- **Original amount paid:** $567\n- **Difference due:** **$2,628**\n\nFor reference, the absolute cheapest business combination on those dates (swapping HAT021 for HAT100, SEA→JFK) would total $2,613 — but that requires changing a flight segment, which isn't permitted on a basic economy booking.\n\n**Payment note:** the $2,628 difference must be paid with a single credit card or gift card already on your profile. Your gift cards hold $198 and $129, so you'd need to use one of your cards (Visa ending 2395 or Mastercard ending 9363).\n\nWould you like me to proceed with the business class upgrade on the existing flights? If so, please confirm **yes** and let me know which payment method to use."}, "resultat": "I understand that basic economy cannot be changed. In that case, I'd like to cancel the current reservation and book a new one. I still want the cheapest business class round trip for the same dates, with or without direct flights.\n\nFor payment, I'd like to use my certificates first, then my gift cards, and cover the rest with my Mastercard. Could you please tell me how much my Mastercard would be charged for this new booking? I do not need baggage or insurance.\n\nAlso, I will only book the new flight if it results in less charges to my Mastercard than what was charged for the original flight.", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 10, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-27T12:03:56.206649Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "The cheapest business-class round trip for the same dates is:\n\n- **JFK → SFO:** HAT023 on 2024-05-26 — **$364** per passenger  \n- **SFO → SEA:** HAT204 on 2024-05-28 — **$248** per passenger  \n- **SEA → JFK:** HAT100 on 2024-05-28 — **$259** per passenger  \n\n**Total per passenger:** $871  \n**Total for 3 passengers:** **$2,613**\n\nOne important payment restriction: a reservation can use **at most one travel certificate**, so I cannot apply all three certificates to the new booking.\n\nUsing the largest certificate and both gift cards:\n\n- Certificate: **$500**\n- Gift cards: **$198 + $129 = $327**\n- Remaining balance: **$1,786**\n\nSo your **Mastercard would be charged $1,786**, which is **more than the original $567 charge**.\n\nEven if the original $567 refund is later returned to your gift card and then used, the Mastercard charge would still be **$1,219**, which is still more than $567.\n\nBecause your condition is that the new booking must result in a **lower Mastercard charge than the original $567**, I should not book the new flight.\n\nIf you still want to cancel reservation **K1NW8N** only, please confirm: **“Yes, cancel K1NW8N for a change of plan.”**"}, "resultat": "Thank you for checking. Since the Mastercard charge would be higher, I will not proceed with booking the new flight.\n\nHowever, I would still like to cancel reservation K1NW8N for a change of plan.", "erreur": null}
